everyday_wordings.plain, line 1: Write "ask "Your name?" and call it person" instead.

    ask "Your name?" and call the answer person
    ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
Try this:
    ask "Your name?" and call it person
Why: Plain says "and call it" to keep what a step gives back.

everyday_wordings.plain, line 2: Write "wait for Enter" instead.

    wait for the Enter key
    ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
Try this:
    wait for Enter
Why: Plain says "wait for Enter" to wait until you press the Enter key.

everyday_wordings.plain, line 4: Write "skip to the next round" instead.

        go to the next round
        ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
Try this:
        skip to the next round
Why: Plain says "skip to the next round" to go straight to the next round of the repeat.

everyday_wordings.plain, line 7: Write "if that fails" instead.

    if that doesn't work
    ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
Try this:
    if that fails
Why: Plain says "if that fails" for the steps to take when a step under "try" has a problem.

